  "needs": {
    "container": true,
    "reason": "the compile database comes from cmake configure, which runs the project's CMake scripts; Daodan runs builds only in a container"
  },
  "traps": [
    "three build systems describe the same two artifacts: CMakeLists.txt (tinyxml2 and xmltest), meson.build (library tinyxml2 and executable xmltest) and a plain Makefile (libtinyxml2.a and xmltest); each is a unit of its own kind at the root",
    "test/CMakeLists.txt is a separate CMake project (tinyxml2-test) that builds ../xmltest.cpp against an installed tinyxml2 found with find_package(tinyxml2 REQUIRED): an external dependency on the package this repository builds, which CI installs first with cmake --install",
    "the CMake library is static or shared by BUILD_SHARED_LIBS (or tinyxml2_SHARED_LIBS); its defines are generator expressions: TINYXML2_DEBUG only in Debug, TINYXML2_IMPORT only for consumers of a shared build, TINYXML2_EXPORT as DEFINE_SYMBOL, _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS only with MSVC, _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 always",
    "xmltest under CMake exists only when tinyxml2_BUILD_TESTING is on (default BUILD_TESTING from include(CTest)); under Meson only with the tests option (default true)",
    "tinyxml2.h is C++ (namespace tinyxml2, classes) although .h is also a C and Objective-C extension; its classes carry the export macro TINYXML2_LIB (class TINYXML2_LIB XMLNode)",
    "contrib/html5-printer.cpp is compiled by no build",
    "no C++ standard is declared by any build file",
    "docs/ is Doxygen output (HTML, JavaScript, CSS) checked in; dox is the Doxygen configuration; resources/ holds XML test inputs that xmltest reads from the working directory",
    "setversion.py is a release helper that rewrites the version in the sources and build files; it is not part of any build",
    "CI runs a matrix of three operating systems and two CMake versions (3.15 and the latest 3.x), with Ninja"
  ]
}
